GITHUB PAGES - three things the repo now has or needs:
  .nojekyll   DONE. Stops Jekyll processing the repo. Without it the .md files
              get rendered as pages and anything starting with _ is dropped.
  404.html    DONE. Uses root-absolute paths (/styles.css) because Pages serves it
              at whatever depth was typed; relative paths would break. Side effect:
              this one page looks wrong opened from the file system. Check it served.
  CNAME       STILL NEEDED. Either set the custom domain in Settings > Pages (which
              writes the file for you) or commit a CNAME containing just the bare
              domain, no https and no trailing slash. Then tick "Enforce HTTPS"
              once the certificate has been issued - it can take a few minutes.
              Add the DNS records at the registrar first, or the check fails.

